  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The additively manufactured Al0.2Co1.5CrFeNi1.5Ti0.3 alloy has a primarily FCC matrix.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The AM starting material has a fine microstructure characteristic of additive manufacturing.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature degradation is governed by the formation and evolution of a continuous Cr/Ti-rich oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective oxidation of Cr and Ti forms an initially protective oxide layer in oxidizing environments.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prolonged exposure causes diffusion-limited depletion of Cr and Ti beneath the surface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Subsurface Cr and Ti depletion leads to internal oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Internal oxidation and protective-element depletion cause embrittlement.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Embrittlement caused by internal oxidation can trigger catastrophic failure.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A reducing atmosphere provides insufficient driving force for continuous protective-scale growth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer formed in a reducing atmosphere will be poor or discontinuous.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A poor or discontinuous oxide layer accelerates internal degradation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidizing conditions will delay failure relative to reducing conditions because of the initially protective scale.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prolonged oxidizing exposure will produce scale spallation or morphological instability.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Scale spallation or morphological instability will lead to catastrophic failure through embrittlement.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing conditions will permit internal oxidation and cause earlier catastrophic failure than oxidizing conditions.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation kinetics become significant for this alloy above approximately 700 °C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exposure for tens to hundreds of hours is sufficient to produce observable Cr and Ti diffusion in this alloy.",
      "field": "boundary",
